  "about": "Word pools for the T5 Oscillator dice. A roll takes a category, draws one entry for each side from that side's pools and writes the two as Impulse A and B, which side gets which decided by the same roll. A side with several pools picks one of them first, each equally likely, then an entry. A pool's suffix is appended to every entry drawn from it: ', c3' puts the generated pitch on C, ', high fidelity field recording' frames a nature scene, and no suffix leaves pitch to the model. 'one attribute changed' instead draws one source and one pair of contrasting words and puts a word in front of the source on each side. 'groove' appends one tempo, drawn per roll, to both sides. Nothing here is tested as a pair: the combinations are new on every roll.",
